GW(){return this.GP("Our quantitative cyber risk assessment research focuses on the systematic evaluation and quantification of cyber risks in maritime cyber-physical systems, including traditional vessels and Maritime Autonomous Surface Ships (MASS). We developed the FMECA-ATT&CK-ATLAS (FAA) framework, which integrates Failure Mode, Effects and Criticality Analysis (FMECA), MITRE ATT&CK, and MITRE ATLAS to model adversarial behavior and quantify cybersecurity risks in maritime cyber-physical systems and autonomous ships. The FAA framework introduces semi-automation into the risk assessment process, reducing reliance on expert judgment, minimizing subjective biases, and significantly decreasing the time and effort required to identify, analyze, and prioritize cybersecurity risks.","FMECA-ATT&CK-ATLAS (FAA)",B.DQ,"assets/images/quantitative-risk.jpg",B.FT,"Quantitative Cyber Risk Assessment")},
